## Synapse Knowledge Layer Sync

The files in `G:\HOUDINI21_RAG_SYSTEM` are the **source of truth**. To sync with Synapse's embedded knowledge:

1. **Synapse semantic_index.json** (`Synapse/rag/documentation/_metadata/semantic_index.json`) needs matching entries using Synapse's simpler format (summary, description, keywords, reference_file)
2. **Synapse reference files** (`Synapse/rag/skills/houdini21-reference/`) should be expanded or new files added
3. The Synapse `KnowledgeIndex` auto-loads on startup -- no code changes needed after files are in place

### Synapse Format Translation

The RAG system uses a richer schema (YAML frontmatter, agent_relevance with scores, common_queries, performance_notes). Synapse's `KnowledgeIndex` uses a simpler format. Here's the translation for each new topic:

```json
// Add to Synapse/rag/documentation/_metadata/semantic_index.json
{
  "vex_functions": {
    "summary": "VEX function reference: 150+ signatures across geometry, math, noise, strings, channels, arrays",
    "description": "Complete VEX function signatures organized by category. Geometry read: point/prim/vertex/detail, attribsize, hasattrib. Write: setpointattrib, setprimattrib, addattrib. Create/delete: addpoint, addprim, addvertex, removepoint, removeprim. Spatial: nearpoint, nearpoints, pcfind, pcfind_radius, pcopen, pcfilter, intersect, xyzdist. Connectivity: neighbours, pointprims, primpoints. Math: sin/cos, pow, sqrt, clamp, fit, lerp, smooth, chramp. Noise: noise, snoise, xnoise, curlnoise, flownoise, vnoise. Vector/matrix: length, normalize, dot, cross, maketransform, cracktransform, quaternion, qrotate. String: sprintf, split, join, match, re_match. Channel: ch, chf, chi, chs, chv, chramp. Array: len, append, find, sort, sum, avg.",
    "keywords": ["vex", "function", "signature", "pcfind", "noise", "lerp", "fit", "addpoint", "nearpoint", "chramp", "channel", "math", "string", "array"],
    "reference_file": "vex-functions-expanded"
  },
  "vex_attributes": {
    "summary": "VEX attribute system: built-in attributes, type prefixes, groups, intrinsics",
    "description": "VEX attribute access patterns. Built-in point attributes: @P (position), @N (normal), @Cd (color), @v (velocity), @pscale, @orient, @id, @age, @life, @rest, @uv. Context variables: @ptnum, @numpt, @primnum, @numprim, @vtxnum. Globals: @Time, @Frame. Type prefixes: f@ float, i@ int, v@ vector, u@ vector2, p@ vector4, s@ string, 2@/3@/4@ matrices. Groups: i@group_name = 1/0, inpointgroup(). Intrinsics: primintrinsic(0, 'measuredarea', @primnum). Promotion: point-to-detail via loops, detail-to-point broadcast, nearest-point transfer via pcfind.",
    "keywords": ["vex", "attribute", "@P", "@N", "@Cd", "point", "prim", "vertex", "detail", "group", "prefix", "type", "intrinsic", "transfer"],
    "reference_file": "vex-attributes"
  },
  "vex_types": {
    "summary": "VEX data types: int, float, vector, matrix, quaternion, string, array; conversions",
    "description": "VEX type system. Scalars: int (32-bit), float (32-bit), string. Vectors: vector2 (2f), vector (3f/xyz), vector4 (4f/quaternion). Matrices: matrix2 (2x2), matrix3 (3x3, rotation/scale), matrix (4x4, full transform). Implicit promotion: int->float->vector2->vector->vector4. Explicit: int(), float(), set(x,y,z). Component access: v.x/.y/.z or v[0]/[1]/[2]. Quaternion ops: quaternion(angle, axis), eulertoquaternion(), qrotate(), slerp(), qmultiply(), qinvert(). Matrix ops: ident(), maketransform(), cracktransform(), invert(), transpose(), lookat(), dihedral().",
    "keywords": ["vex", "type", "conversion", "cast", "vector", "matrix", "quaternion", "vector4", "matrix3", "int", "float", "string", "array"],
    "reference_file": "vex-types"
  },
  "vex_performance": {
    "summary": "VEX optimization: fast/slow patterns, spatial queries, memory, profiling",
    "description": "VEX performance patterns. Fast: pcfind (KD-tree O(log n)) over nearpoints (O(n)). Use distance2/length2 (avoid sqrt). Cache @-reads outside loops. Use smooth/lerp for branchless blends. Pre-size arrays with resize(). Slow: string attribute lookups in loops, dynamic array growth, complex branching. Run-over selection: Points for per-point, Detail + explicit loops for small geo with inter-element deps. Compilation: first cook compiles, ch() changes don't trigger recompile. Profile via Performance Monitor. Common bottlenecks: O(n^2) spatial query, memory spikes from per-element arrays, string lookups in loops.",
    "keywords": ["vex", "performance", "optimization", "speed", "slow", "fast", "bottleneck", "pcfind", "distance2", "parallel", "memory", "compile"],
    "reference_file": "vex-performance"
  },
  "vex_patterns": {
    "summary": "VEX code patterns: deformation, color, generation, grouping, solver, transfer",
    "description": "15+ copy-paste VEX patterns. Deformation: sine wave, noise displacement along normal, twist, taper via chramp. Color: by height (chramp), by curvature (neighbour dot products), random per piece (hsvtorgb). Generation: spiral points (detail wrangle), polyline from points, grid from scratch. Grouping: by bounding box, by normal direction (dot product threshold), every Nth point. Solver: point advection with gravity/ground collision, attribute decay (frame-rate independent). Transfer: nearest-point attribute transfer, distance-weighted blend via pcfind, smooth/relax points (neighbour averaging), edge detection (gradient magnitude).",
    "keywords": ["vex", "pattern", "example", "snippet", "deform", "color", "noise", "spiral", "wave", "group", "solver", "transfer", "smooth", "relax"],
    "reference_file": "vex-patterns"
  }
}
```

